      "narration": "Let's solve x squared plus two x minus three equals zero using the quadratic formula.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1100,
      "in": [
        {
          "t": "label",
          "text": "x² + 2x − 3 = 0",
          "space": "canvas",
          "at": [
            0.5,
            0.24
          ],
          "anchor": "center",
          "size": 23,
          "color": "accent",
          "anim": "fade"
        }
      ],
      "claim_tags": [
        "visual_step_1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The quadratic formula gives x in terms of a, b and c.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1100,
      "in": [
        {
          "t": "label",
          "text": "x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / 2a",
          "space": "canvas",
          "at": [
            0.5,
            0.372
          ],
          "anchor": "center",
          "size": 17,
          "color": "ink",
          "anim": "fade"
        }
      ],
      "claim_tags": [
        "visual_step_2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Here a is one, b is two, and c is minus three.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1100,
      "in": [
        {
          "t": "label",
          "text": "a = 1,  b = 2,  c = −3",
          "space": "canvas",
          "at": [
            0.5,
            0.504
          ],
          "anchor": "center",
          "size": 20,
          "color": "ink",
          "anim": "fade"
        }
      ],
      "claim_tags": [
        "visual_step_3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Substitute those values into the formula.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1100,
      "in": [
        {
          "t": "label",
          "text": "x = (−2 ± √(2² − 4·1·(−3))) / 2",
          "space": "canvas",
          "at": [
            0.5,
            0.636
          ],
          "anchor": "center",
          "size": 17,
          "color": "ink",
          "anim": "fade"
        }
      ],
      "claim_tags": [
        "visual_step_4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Under the root, four plus twelve is sixteen, whose square root is four.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1100,
      "in": [
        {
          "t": "label",
          "text": "x = (−2 ± 4) / 2",
          "space": "canvas",
          "at": [
            0.5,
            0.768
          ],
          "anchor": "center",
          "size": 23,
          "color": "ink",
          "anim": "fade"
        }
      ],
      "claim_tags": [
        "visual_step_5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "So the two roots are x equals one and x equals minus three.",
      "anim_ms": 600,
      "hold_ms": 1800,
      "in": [
